{"step_index":159,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T23:27:33Z","thinking":"The file `story000_script.rpf` appears to be encrypted, likely with RAGE NG/AES. Examining `GTAVI_MISSION_FLOW1.jpg` reveals a flow chart. The image requires transcription of the nodes and connections, followed by careful extraction of all text elements to understand the mission flow.\n\n\nTranscription reveals a multi-branched mission flow with textual and call-based triggers. Several branches center around financial transactions and character interactions, indicated by mail, calls, and mission titles. Conditional paths exist, influencing mission progression, such as a \"Just a Scratch\" decision impacting later calls.\n\n\nThe mission flow has been fully transcribed from the image, revealing conditional branches and key interactions. Identified the final mission node as \"DON GONE\" within the provided flowchart image. Noticed critical missions are missing from Chapter 1 and entire chapters 2-5 are absent from the transcribed flow.\n\n\nThe analysis focuses on speedrun optimization, specifically identifying parallel execution opportunities and time skips. Discovered that the *Feng Shui* 24-hour wait provides an opening to run *Unwanted Attention* and *Gear Up* missions simultaneously. Mailbox cash pickups offer a passive early-game income source totaling $1,540.\n\nIdentified several skippable tasks like *Get Haircut* and *Kenton Treasure Search* that offer no benefit for an Any% speedrun. Noted mandatory mission gates, specifically *Just a Scratch*, which must be completed prior to *Day Release*.\n\n\nSpeedrun optimization strategies continue, focusing on mission order and time-saving techniques. Prioritized key missions and character unlocks in Chapter 2, specifically *Coffee Break* for character switching. Examined Chapter 3 heist prep, evaluating the cost-benefit of optional objectives like tower destruction in relation to total time and required haul.\n\nChapter 4 optimization centers on the $75,000 requirement for *Party Hard*, highlighting the need to conserve funds from the Chapter 3 heist to avoid side tasks.\n\n\n*Headliners* mission is mandatory for airport setup unlocks. Within *VCIA Takedown*, obtain *Francisco's LMG-6* during the shootout for enhanced efficiency at the airport. *Sunset* marks the point of no return for Chapter 5; trigger it without delay to avoid unnecessary delays.\n\nFor the fastest ending in an Any% speedrun, immediately select \"PROCEED\" in *Protective Custody*. *Ending B (The Deal)* or *Ending C (The Sacrifice)* are optimal due to *Ending A's* costly $2,000,000 and relationship requirements, which add substantial time to the run through non-essential side tasks.\n\n\nAnalyzing the new diagram, it appears to be a much more comprehensive mission flow, detailing the entire game up to Chapter 5 with expanded information. The inclusion of speedrun-specific elements like skip badges and timing notes offers crucial optimizations. Examined the markdown guide; it should provide all necessary routing details, time skips, and mission orders for the Any% run.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Python generator to render the enhanced Speedrun Flowchart for Chapter 1 and the Full Campaign Speedrun Routing Diagram in the visual style of GTAVI_MISSION_FLOW1.jpg.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.patches as patches\nimport os\nimport shutil\n\nWORKSPACE_DIR = r\"C:\\Users\\<user>\\Downloads\\GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK\"\nARTIFACT_DIR = r\"C:\\Users\\<user>\\.gemini\\antigravity-cli\\brain\\96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c\"\n\nBG_COLOR = \"#2e3035\"       # Similar to reference dark gray\nTEXT_COLOR = \"#000000\"\n\ndef draw_mission(ax, x, y, w, h, title, subtitle=\"\", is_climax=False, is_gate=False):\n    bg = \"#fef08a\" if not is_climax else \"#fed7aa\"\n    border = \"#ca8a04\" if not is_climax else \"#ea580c\"\n    lw = 2.0 if (is_climax or is_gate) else 1.2\n    \n    rect = patches.Rectangle(\n        (x, y), w, h,\n        linewidth=lw,\n        edgecolor=border,\n        facecolor=bg,\n        zorder=3\n    )\n    ax.add_patch(rect)\n    \n    ty = y + h/2 + 0.12 if subtitle else y + h/2\n    ax.text(x + w/2, ty, title, ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=8.5, fontweight=\"bold\", color=\"#1c1917\", zorder=4)\n    if subtitle:\n        ax.text(x + w/2, y + 0.2, subtitle, ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=7.0, color=\"#44403c\", zorder=4)\n\ndef draw_callout(ax, x, y, w, h, text, icon_type=\"text\", badge=\"\"):\n    # icon_type: \"phone\", \"text\", \"mailbox\", \"cash\"\n    rect = patches.Rectangle(\n        (x, y), w, h,\n        linewidth=1.0,\n        edgecolor=\"#71717a\",\n        facecolor=\"#ffffff\",\n        zorder=3\n    )\n    ax.add_patch(rect)\n    \n    icon_str = \"\"\n    if icon_type == \"phone\":\n        icon_str = \"[☎ CALL] \"\n    elif icon_type == \"text\":\n        icon_str = \"[✉ MSG] \"\n    elif icon_type == \"mailbox\":\n        icon_str = \"[📭 MAIL] \"\n    elif icon_type == \"cash\":\n        icon_str = \"[💰 CASH] \"\n        \n    full_text = icon_str + text\n    ax.text(x + w/2, y + h/2, full_text, ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=7.2, fontweight=\"bold\" if icon_type==\"phone\" else \"normal\", color=\"#09090b\", zorder=4)\n\ndef draw_heart(ax, x, y, w, h, text, skip_tag=True):\n    # Relationship / Domestic Task\n    rect = patches.Rectangle(\n        (x, y), w, h,\n        linewidth=1.2,\n        edgecolor=\"#f43f5e\",\n        facecolor=\"#ffe4e6\",\n        zorder=3\n    )\n    ax.add_patch(rect)\n    heart_text = \"♥ \" + text\n    if skip_tag:\n        heart_text += \"\\n[ANY% SKIP]\"\n    ax.text(x + w/2, y + h/2, heart_text, ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=6.8, fontweight=\"bold\", color=\"#9f1239\", zorder=4)\n\ndef draw_side(ax, x, y, w, h, text, skip_tag=True):\n    # Purple side activity\n    rect = patches.Rectangle(\n        (x, y), w, h,\n        linewidth=1.2,\n        edgecolor=\"#a855f7\",\n        facecolor=\"#f3e8ff\",\n        zorder=3\n    )\n    ax.add_patch(rect)\n    side_text = text\n    if skip_tag:\n        side_text += \"\\n[OPTIONAL / SKIP]\"\n    ax.text(x + w/2, y + h/2, side_text, ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=6.8, color=\"#581c87\", zorder=4)\n\ndef draw_diamond(ax, cx, cy, r, text):\n    pts = [[cx, cy + r], [cx + r*1.6, cy], [cx, cy - r], [cx - r*1.6, cy]]\n    poly = patches.Polygon(pts, closed=True, linewidth=1.5, edgecolor=\"#cbd5e1\", facecolor=\"#ffffff\", zorder=3)\n    ax.add_patch(poly)\n    ax.text(cx, cy, text, ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=6.8, fontweight=\"bold\", color=\"#0f172a\", zorder=4)\n\ndef draw_speedrun_note(ax, x, y, w, h, title, note):\n    rect = patches.Rectangle(\n        (x, y), w, h,\n        linewidth=1.5,\n        edgecolor=\"#10b981\",\n        facecolor=\"#064e3b\",\n        zorder=3\n    )\n    ax.add_patch(rect)\n    ax.text(x + w/2, y + h - 0.22, \"⚡ SPEEDRUN OPTIMIZATION\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=7.5, fontweight=\"bold\", color=\"#34d399\", zorder=4)\n    ax.text(x + w/2, y + h/2 - 0.1, note, ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=6.8, color=\"#ecfdf5\", zorder=4)\n\ndef draw_arrow(ax, p1, p2, color=\"#ffffff\", lw=1.2, rad=0.0):\n    conn = f\"arc3,rad={rad}\" if rad != 0 else \"arc3,rad=0\"\n    ax.annotate(\n        \"\",\n        xy=p2, xytext=p1,\n        arrowprops=dict(\n            arrowstyle=\"->,head_width=0.25,head_length=0.35\",\n            color=color,\n            lw=lw,\n            shrinkA=3,\n            shrinkB=3,\n            connectionstyle=conn\n        ),\n        zorder=2\n    )\n\nprint(\"Speedrun flowchart primitives initialized.\")\n","Description":"Primitive drawing functions for speedrunning mission flowchart in reference style","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\<user>\\.gemini\\antigravity-cli\\brain\\96252013-4633-45e8-b6a2-59b18be9e68c\\scratch\\speedrun_primitives.py","toolAction":"Writing speedrun flowchart primitives","toolSummary":"Create speedrun primitives script"}}]}
